        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Incline walking can help you lose thigh fat only by helping you
            lose fat overall — and it is very good at that.</strong> It raises the energy cost of a
            walk without the impact of running, works the glutes, hamstrings and calves, and is easy
            enough to repeat most days. It will not make your legs bulky.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Build the grade gradually, keep your hands off the rails, add two short strength sessions a
            week, and judge the thighs over months rather than weeks. For the energy-cost, heart-rate
            and joint side of things, see
            <a href="/what-does-incline-walking-do/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">what incline walking does</a>.
          </p>
